{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:unit-normal-of-orientation-smooth","title":"prop:unit-normal-of-orientation-smooth","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1914,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:unit-normal-of-orientation-smooth","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal-of-orientation]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-unit-normal-field]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-orientation]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:interior-multiplication]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:unit-normal-of-orientation-smooth","line":3095,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[The Normal Determined by an Orientation Is Smooth]\n\\label{prop:unit-normal-of-orientation-smooth}\n\n\\uses{def:unit-normal-of-orientation, def:smooth-unit-normal-field, def:smooth-orientation, lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame, lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth, lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos, lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal, prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal, def:interior-multiplication}\n\n\n\n\nIf the ambient and hypersurface orientations are smooth, the unit normal determined by the hypersurface orientation is a smooth global unit normal field.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame,lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth,lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos,lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal,prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal}\n\\sketch Near $p$, choose a smooth positive tangent frame and a smooth local unit normal $W$. The smooth nonzero function $s(x)=((W\\lrcorner dV_{\\widetilde g})|_M)_x(E_1,\\ldots,E_n)$ has constant sign on a smaller neighbourhood. The determined normal equals $W$ where $s>0$ and $-W$ where $s<0$, hence is smooth.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[The Normal Determined by an Orientation Is Smooth] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a756e69742d6e6f726d616c2d6f662d6f7269656e746174696f6e2d736d6f6f7468\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aunit-normal-of-orientation\">↗ def:unit-normal-of-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-unit-normal-field\">↗ def:smooth-unit-normal-field</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-orientation\">↗ def:smooth-orientation</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anormal-space-orthonormal-frame\">↗ lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anormal-restrict-frame-smooth\">↗ lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aoriented-unit-normal-iff-pos\">↗ lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anormal-restrict-neg-normal\">↗ lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aexistsunique-oriented-unit-normal\">↗ prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ainterior-multiplication\">↗ def:interior-multiplication</a> <p></p>If the ambient and hypersurface orientations are smooth, the unit normal determined by the hypersurface orientation is a smooth global unit normal field.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anormal-space-orthonormal-frame\">↗ lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anormal-restrict-frame-smooth\">↗ lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aoriented-unit-normal-iff-pos\">↗ lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Anormal-restrict-neg-normal\">↗ lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aexistsunique-oriented-unit-normal\">↗ prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal</a> \\sketch Near <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span>, choose a smooth positive tangent frame and a smooth local unit normal <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W$\">$W$</span>. The smooth nonzero function <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s(x)=((W\\lrcorner dV_{\\widetilde g})|_M)_x(E_1,\\ldots ,E_n)$\">$s(x)=((W\\lrcorner dV_{\\widetilde g})|_M)_x(E_1,\\ldots ,E_n)$</span> has constant sign on a smaller neighbourhood. The determined normal equals <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W$\">$W$</span> where <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s&gt;0$\">$s&gt;0$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$-W$\">$-W$</span> where <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$s&lt;0$\">$s&lt;0$</span>, hence is smooth. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal-of-orientation","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-volume-form-only-if","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal-of-orientation","title":"def:unit-normal-of-orientation","label":"def:unit-normal-of-orientation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-unit-normal-field","title":"def:smooth-unit-normal-field","label":"def:smooth-unit-normal-field"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-orientation","title":"def:smooth-orientation","label":"def:smooth-orientation"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame","title":"lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame","label":"lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth","title":"lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth","label":"lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos","title":"lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos","label":"lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal","title":"lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal","label":"lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal","title":"prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal","label":"prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:interior-multiplication","title":"def:interior-multiplication","label":"def:interior-multiplication"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-volume-form-only-if","title":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form-only-if","label":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form-only-if"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hypersurface-volume-form","title":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form","label":"prop:hypersurface-volume-form"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:unit-normal-of-orientation-smooth","title":"prop:unit-normal-of-orientation-smooth","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[The Normal Determined by an Orientation Is Smooth]\n\\label{prop:unit-normal-of-orientation-smooth}\n\n\\uses{def:unit-normal-of-orientation, def:smooth-unit-normal-field, def:smooth-orientation, lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame, lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth, lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos, lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal, prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal, def:interior-multiplication}\n\n\n\n\nIf the ambient and hypersurface orientations are smooth, the unit normal determined by the hypersurface orientation is a smooth global unit normal field.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame,lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth,lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos,lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal,prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal}\n\\sketch Near $p$, choose a smooth positive tangent frame and a smooth local unit normal $W$. The smooth nonzero function $s(x)=((W\\lrcorner dV_{\\widetilde g})|_M)_x(E_1,\\ldots,E_n)$ has constant sign on a smaller neighbourhood. The determined normal equals $W$ where $s>0$ and $-W$ where $s<0$, hence is smooth.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal-of-orientation","title":"def:unit-normal-of-orientation","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-unit-normal-field","title":"def:smooth-unit-normal-field","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-orientation","title":"def:smooth-orientation","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame","title":"lem:normal-space-orthonormal-frame","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth","title":"lem:normal-restrict-frame-smooth","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos","title":"lem:oriented-unit-normal-iff-pos","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal","title":"lem:normal-restrict-neg-normal","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal","title":"prop:existsunique-oriented-unit-normal","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:interior-multiplication","title":"def:interior-